    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0226" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856.001W64/54: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Canada</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Simmons</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-10T12:00:00-04:00">June 10,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 10—11:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. I am reliably informed in confidence from high governmental source that
                    Queen Wilhelmina and certain other members of Nether-land Royal Family will
                    arrive by British destroyer in Canada approximately today.<anchor n="71"
                        xml:id="d172-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Simmons</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For note from the German Foreign Office requesting the United States to
                        withdraw the diplomatic missions in Norway, the Netherlands, Belgium, and
                        Luxemburg, see telegram No. 2223, July 1, 10 a.m., from the Chargé in
                        Germany, <ref target="#pg174">page 174</ref>. For Department’s instructions
                        to close the missions, effective not later than July 15, 1940, see telegram
                        No. 1856, July 4, noon, <ref target="#pg175">page 175</ref>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d172-f1" n="71" xml:id="d172-f1-content">
                <p>Crown Princess Juliana of the Netherlands and her two children arrived in Canada
                    on June 11, 1940, to stay in Ottawa for duration of the war. Queen Wilhelmina
                    remained in England with her Government.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
